# $Id: dcd.users,v 1.9 2006/10/18 10:51:51 rav Exp $
#
# You can add an administration account here.
# Format of each line:
# "login:password:e-mail:description:permissions"
# or just: "login:" if you only want to prevent users from using this nick.
#
# permissions:
#	c - access to the telnet console
#		- can be used with any other priviledge
#
#	s - superior user
#		- mislots/minshare is not tested
#		- ignores search_interval
#		- can't be used with 'a' or 'n' priviledge
#		- user can kick/redirect user but not 's' user 
#
#	a - administrator
#		- can't be used with 's' or 'n' priviledge
#		- user can kick/redirect 'n' users but not any of 's' or 'a' users 
#		
#	n - just reserving nick
#		- can be used also with c priviledge
#
#   p - allows user to be in passive mode when allow_passive is set to 0
#		- can be used with any other priviledge
#
#	m - checkout for minsshare is disabled for this user
#		- can be used with any other priviledge
#
#	r - checkout for minslots is disabled for this user
#		- can be used with any other priviledge
#
#	f - allows user to specify his IP in client. Used when user wants to be ACTIVE, 
#       but he is behind NAT and wants to forward port. Used only when allow_forwarding 
#		in dcd.conf is set to 0
#		- can be used with any other priviledge
#
#	i - user can search without waiting search_interval
#
# Empty lines or beginning with `#' are ignored.

admin:changeme:admin@localhost:DC Administrator:cs
